 ## Receipt taxonomy — every removal needs exactly one
 
-| Receipt | Qualifies when | Counting / verification command |
+No `git fetch`. A configured `origin` URL with zero `refs/remotes/origin/*`
+is not a pushed receipt. A local ref (`refs/heads/master`, `refs/heads/main`)
+never is. Fleet default, measured 2026-10-18: `origin/master`, not
+`origin/main` (`git symbolic-ref --short refs/remotes/origin/HEAD`).
+
+| Receipt | Qualifies when | Verification |
 |---|---|---|
-| `pushed` | after `git fetch`, the commit carrying the artifact passes `git merge-base --is-ancestor <commit> origin/<branch>` | `git fetch -q && git merge-base --is-ancestor <commit> origin/main && echo PUSHED` |
-| `moved-to-obsidian` | a matching row exists in `corpus/knowledge/obsidian-ledger.tsv` with source path + sha256 AND vault path + sha256 | `awk -F'\t' -v p="<relpath>" '$1==p{print}' corpus/knowledge/obsidian-ledger.tsv` then `sha256sum` both sides |
-| `stale` | known scratch type (`.scratch/`, `*.tmp`, checkpoint blobs, `out/`, `reports/round-*/**-draft.*`), nothing references it (`rg --files-with-matches <name>` across the owning repo returns 0 live hits), AND mtime older than the owning lane's last admitted round | `find <path> -newermt <last-round-date> | wc -l` == 0 and `rg -l <basename> <repo>` == 0 |
+| `pushed` | The path exists. Its introducing commit (`git log --diff-filter=A --format=%H -1 -- <path>`) is an ancestor of the remote-tracking default ref. Resolve that ref as the tools do: `git symbolic-ref --quiet --short refs/remotes/origin/HEAD`, strip the `origin/` prefix, and require `refs/remotes/origin/<name>` to exist; else the single `refs/remotes/origin/*` branch ref when exactly one exists. Otherwise this receipt does not qualify. | `bash tools/souji-verify.sh <path>` prints `SAFE` / `pushed`, and `test -e <path>` |
+| `moved-to-obsidian` | A row in `corpus/knowledge/obsidian-ledger.tsv` matches absolute source path + source sha256 and absolute vault path + vault sha256, both re-hashed read-only. Directory digests fail closed if any symlink is in scope. Not a receipt when source path equals vault path, when either path is relative, when either hash is not 64 lowercase hex, or when either path is secret-shaped. The Obsidian CLI is advisory only and is not a receipt. | `bash tools/souji-vault-verify.sh --fallback <path>` prints `VERIFIED(moved-to-obsidian)` |
+| `stale` | Scratch family the tools implement: a `.scratch` path component, or basename `*.out`, `*.log`, `*-draft.*`, `*checkpoint*.json`, `*checkpoint*.png`, `*ckpt*.json`, `*ckpt*.png`, `*.ckpt`, `launch-*.json`. Not `*.tmp`, and not an `out/` directory, by themselves. mtime older than `--stale-days` (default 1; the tools refuse when age ≤ N×86400 seconds). Zero live references from a fixed-string basename sweep that includes hidden files. Exclude `.git`, `souji-shokunin/census/**`, `souji-shokunin/tests/**`, and `**/.ufo-quarantine/**`. A hit under `.ufo/**` still counts. | The agent sweep below. A tool `SAFE(stale)` is not sufficient by itself (residual R1) |
+| `metadata-prune` | A non-main worktree registration whose directory is absent, whose tip has 0 commits not already reachable from `--all`, and whose named branch has 0 commits not in `--remotes`. The named-branch check runs first: an absent directory does not prune an unpushed branch. | `bash tools/souji-verify.sh <worktree-path>` prints `SAFE` / `metadata-prune` |
 
